<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dipendra of Nepal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a>–<a href="/years/2001">2001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Crown Prince Dipendra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dipendra (1971–2001) was the crown prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birendra-of-nepal">King Birendra</a>. On 1 June 2001, at a family gathering in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narayanhiti-palace">Narayanhiti Palace</a>, he shot dead his father, his mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aishwarya-of-nepal">Queen Aishwarya</a> and other members of the royal family, according to the official inquiry, before shooting himself. He was proclaimed king while in a coma and died three days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dipendra-of-nepal.jpg" alt="Dipendra of Nepal" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nabin K. Sapkota · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crown_Prince_Dependra_Bikram_Shah_Dev.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
